ication (unfriendly), responsibility unknown, adaptability (not open to new ideas, show-off).\n\nD: reliability unknown, stress resilience (responds adequately to unexpected events), technical competence (solves problems extremely well, concentration), decision quality unknown, attention (concentrates well), crew cooperation (moody, loner), professional communication unknown, responsibility (takes responsibility seriously), adaptability unknown.\n\nWe need to decide best overall. The panel hasn't covered reliability for C and D. But we have no evidence of reliability for them. B is very conscientious (reliability). A is 100% reliable. So reliability is strong for A and B. C and D unknown.\n\nCommunication: A difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric. B pretentious, wrong tone. C unfriendly, show-off, not open to new ideas. D moody, loner.\n\nStress: B handles stress well. C anticipates dangerous situations (implies stress resilience). D responds adequately. A unknown.\n\nTechnical: B good at weather, computer skills. C sees complex connections, spatial vision. D solves problems extremely well, concentration.\n\nDecision quality: A quick correct decisions. Others unknown.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. A positive atmosphere maybe indicates responsibility. B unknown. C unknown.\n\nAdaptability: A not willing to further education (low). B unknown. C not open to new ideas (low). D unknown.\n\nOverall, A has strong reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and low adaptability. B has strong reliability, stress, technical, but communication tone issues. C has strong technical and anticipation, leadership, but communication and adaptability issues, and unknown reliability. D has responsibility, problem solving, but communication and reliability unknown.\n\nWhich candidate best fits overall? Likely B or A. A's communication difficulty could be severe. B's pretentious tone also severe. Which is more manageable? Possibly B's issues are more about tone, can be trained. A's difficulty communicating ideas may affect safety-critical communication. Also A not willing to further education, which is a problem for long-distance pilot needing ongoing training. So B may be better.\n\nThus I might keep my vote for B, but need to respond to Agent 2's recommendation for C, and discuss. I can argue that while C's anticipation and leadership are strong, the lack of evidence for reliability and adaptability, plus unfriendly and not open to new ideas, are serious concerns. B's reliability and stress handling are more critical. So I maintain B.\n\nThus my public message: I acknowledge Agent 2's points, but I remain convinced B is best. Provide evidence: B very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Acknowledge communication issues but argue they are manageable. Compare to C's lack of reliability evidence and poor adaptability. Conclude vote for B.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
